Resthiopha Game - Technical Documentation
Overview
Resthiopha Game is a 2D tile-based RPG built using Java Swing for GUI and Spring Boot for backend support. The player can move on a grid, fight monsters, collect loot, and manage inventory.
Project Structure
- api → REST API layer
  - controller → REST endpoints
  - model → DTO/Entity models
  - repository → Database access
  - service → Business logic
- entity → Game entities (player, monster)
- main → Game screen, loop, input
- tile → Map system and drawing
- resources → map.txt and Spring Boot configs
Technologies
- Java 17+
- Java Swing
- Spring Boot 3
- H2 Database
- Maven / Gradle
Player Controls
- W A S D → Movement
- I → Toggle inventory
- Q → Equip item
- E → Sell item
- Y / N → Game Over options
Game Mechanics
- Monsters move randomly or toward the player
- Monsters attack if nearby
- Loot: sword or shoes
- Better gear is auto-equipped
- Inventory pauses the game
REST API Endpoints
GearController:
- GET /api/items/random → Get random loot
- GET /api/items → Get all loot

PlayerController:
- GET /api/player/coins → Get coin count
- GET /api/player/inventory → Get inventory
- GET /api/player/equipment → Get equipped items
- GET /api/player/summary → Player summary
- GET /api/player → Get player entity
- POST /api/player/save → Save player entity
Map System
- Loaded from map.txt
- '1' / 'X' = Wall
- '0' / '.' = Path
- 'P' = Player start position
Database
- H2 in-memory database
- H2 Console: /h2-console
- PlayerEntity is mapped via @Entity
Startup Instructions
1. Start Spring Boot: ResthiophaGameApplication
2. Launch game window: Main
