Resthiopha Game - Code Responsibility Summary
Main.java
• Initializes JFrame and adds GamePanel
• Configures window settings and starts game loop
GamePanel.java
• Defines screen and tile size
• Handles game loop, monster respawn
• Draws all game elements
Monster.java
• Implements monster movement and AI
• Attacks player and respawns after 20s
Player.java
• Manages player movement and collision
• Handles combat with monsters
• Regenerates HP every second
• Manages gear: auto-equip and inventory
• Handles keypress interactions (I/Q/E)
• Draws player and HP bar
TileManager.java
• Loads map.txt and parses it
• Maps tile types (wall, path, player start)
• Draws tile background and wall indicators
Tile.java
• Represents a single tile on the map
• Holds image and collision info
Gear.java
• Represents an item (Sword or Shoes)
• Stores name, type, value and sell price
PlayerEntity.java
• JPA entity for saving player state in database
• Fields: coins, level, currentHp, maxHp
GearService.java
• Provides random gear logic
• Returns loot or all available gear
PlayerService.java
• Handles connection between game and database
• Retrieves or saves PlayerEntity
• Returns current in-game player object
GearController.java
• Exposes endpoints to fetch gear
• GET /api/items/random, /api/items
PlayerController.java
• Exposes endpoints to fetch or update player info
• GET /api/player/coins, inventory, summary, etc.
• POST /api/player/save
KeyHandler.java
• Listens for key presses
• Controls movement and game interactions (I, Q, E, Y/N)
PlayerRepository.java
• Used to store and access data related to the PlayerEntity class in the H2 database
• Inherits from Spring Data JPA’s JpaRepository interface.
• Automatically provides CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete)

 
Development Notes
• Player used to pass through walls - fixed using futureArea collision check
• Movement logic switched from speed-based to pixel-step movement
• Monsters respawn after 20 seconds via RespawnInfo
• Game Over UI prompts Y/N keys
• Connected to Postman by exposing REST endpoints
